    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p20-q4-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$P(x)=x^3+6x^2+11x+6$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x+1)(x+2)(x+3)$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}P(-1)&=-1+6-11+6\\\\P(-1)&=0\\end{align*}$$\n\nThus $x+1$ is a factor. Long division gives quotient $x^2+5x+6$ and remainder 0.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P(x)&=(x+1)(x^2+5x+6)\\\\P(x)&=(x+1)(x+2)(x+3)\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q4-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$P(x)=x^3-7x^2-x+7$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x+1)(x-1)(x-7)$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}P(1)&=1-7-1+7\\\\P(1)&=0\\end{align*}$$\n\nThus $x-1$ is a factor. Long division gives quotient $x^2-6x-7$ and remainder 0.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P(x)&=(x-1)(x^2-6x-7)\\\\P(x)&=(x-1)(x+1)(x-7)\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q4-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$P(x)=x^3+3x^2-13x-15$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x+1)(x+5)(x-3)$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}P(-1)&=-1+3+13-15\\\\P(-1)&=0\\end{align*}$$\n\nThus $x+1$ is a factor. Long division gives quotient $x^2+2x-15$ and remainder 0.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P(x)&=(x+1)(x^2+2x-15)\\\\P(x)&=(x+1)(x+5)(x-3)\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q4-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$P(x)=x^3+x^2-21x-45$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x-5)(x+3)^2$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}P(-3)&=-27+9+63-45\\\\P(-3)&=0\\end{align*}$$\n\nThus $x+3$ is a factor. Long division gives quotient $x^2-2x-15$ and remainder 0.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P(x)&=(x+3)(x^2-2x-15)\\\\P(x)&=(x+3)(x-5)(x+3)\\\\P(x)&=(x-5)(x+3)^2\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q4-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$P(x)=x^3+x^2-5x+3$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x-1)^2(x+3)$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}P(1)&=1+1-5+3\\\\P(1)&=0\\end{align*}$$\n\nThus $x-1$ is a factor. Long division gives quotient $x^2+2x-3$ and remainder 0.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P(x)&=(x-1)(x^2+2x-3)\\\\P(x)&=(x-1)(x-1)(x+3)\\\\P(x)&=(x-1)^2(x+3)\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q4-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$P(x)=x^3+3x^2-4$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x-1)(x+2)^2$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}P(1)&=1+3-4\\\\P(1)&=0\\end{align*}$$\n\nThus $x-1$ is a factor. Long division gives quotient $x^2+4x+4$ and remainder 0.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P(x)&=(x-1)(x^2+4x+4)\\\\P(x)&=(x-1)(x+2)^2\\end{align*}$$",
